and from m1n1 (MIT, Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors): src/pmgr.c (the PMGR
device table walk of kernel/pd_soc.cpp), src/kboot.c (where the digitizer's
calibration is in the Apple device tree), proxyclient/experiments/touchbar_rainbow.py
(the display pipe running with its vertical blank bits on).

kernel/pd_soc.*, kernel/pd_gpio.* and kernel/pd_dart_fixed.* are copies of the files of
the same names in ../m1-sound (see its NOTICE), with an interrupt group argument in
pd_gpio and a power domain lookup by name in pd_soc.

kernel/pd_tb_keys.c and pd_tb_keys.h (the key strip's layout, picture and touch logic),
user/pdtbtest.c, host-test/, guest/ and tools/ are original work under the MIT license.

spihid/ (MIT, original work) is added to PDM1SPIHID.kext, the built-in keyboard's driver of
../m1-keyboard and ../m1-trackpad-child/multitouch, by build-spihid.nix: the place of the
Fn key in the keyboard's reports, read from the keyboard's own report descriptor (the usage
Linux drivers/hid/hid-apple.c takes as KEY_FN: page 0xff, usage 0x03), and the message that
tells PDAppleTouchBar about Fn and typing. The rest of that kext is unchanged and keeps
its own notices.
The strip's layout numbers and colours, its two layers and its idle timeouts are those
of tiny-dfr (https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr, MIT OR Apache-2.0, Copyright The
Asahi Linux Contributors); no code or image of tiny-dfr is included.

Not in this directory and never to be committed: the digitizer's firmware
(private/firmware/apple/dfrmtfw-j293.bin, Apple's, extracted from this machine's own
macOS by the Asahi installer) and its calibration (read at run time from the Apple
device tree).

The text of the MIT licence that m1n1 is under is reproduced in ../m1-sound/NOTICE.
